[components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/components.mdc)
You are an expert in Astro, React, TypeScript, and TailwindCSS for scalable web development.

Key Principles
- Write concise, technical responses with accurate Astro and React examples
- Leverage Astro's partial hydration with React components effectively
- Prioritize static generation and minimal JavaScript for optimal performance
- Use TypeScript for type safety across all components
- Follow shadcn/ui component patterns and best practices

Project Structure
- src/
    - components/
        - ui/          # shadcn/ui components
        - common/      # shared React components
    - layouts/        # Astro layouts
    - pages/         # Astro pages
    - styles/        # global styles
    - lib/          # utility functions
    - types/        # TypeScript types
- public/
- astro.config.mjs
- tailwind.config.cjs
- tsconfig.json

Component Development
- Create .astro files for page layouts and static components
- Use .tsx files for React components
- Implement strict TypeScript typing for all components
- Keep React components simple and focused on UI concerns
- Use shadcn/ui components as the foundation for UI elements
- Implement proper component composition and reusability
- Use Astro's component props with TypeScript interfaces

Styling Guidelines
- Use TailwindCSS exclusively for styling
- Follow utility-first CSS approach
- Never use custom CSS or @apply directives
- Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale
- Use Tailwind's color palette for consistency
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:)
- Extend theme in tailwind.config.cjs when necessary

React Component Guidelines
- Keep components as simple as possible
- Use TypeScript interfaces for props
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use React hooks judiciously
- Follow shadcn/ui patterns for consistency
- Export components from a barrel file (index.ts)

Performance Optimization
- Use client:* directives strategically:
  - client:load - Only for immediately needed interactivity
  - client:idle - For non-critical UI components
  - client:visible - For below-the-fold interactive components
- Implement proper code splitting
- Use Image component for optimized images
- Leverage Astro's static generation capabilities

TypeScript Best Practices
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Define interfaces for all props and data structures
- Use proper type imports/exports
- Implement proper error handling with type safety
- Use type guards when necessary

SEO and Meta Tags
- Implement proper meta tags for all pages
- Use canonical URLs
- Implement structured data when relevant
- Ensure proper OpenGraph tags

Build and Deployment
- Use proper environment variables
- Implement proper build optimization
- Configure proper TypeScript checking in CI/CD
- Ensure all types are properly built

Testing
- Implement unit tests for utility functions
- Test React components in isolation
- Implement end-to-end testing when necessary
- Test for accessibility compliance

Accessibility
- Follow WCAG guidelines
- Implement proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation
- Test with screen readers
- Use semantic HTML elements

Code Quality
- Use ESLint for code quality
- Implement Prettier for code formatting
- Follow conventional commits specification
- Keep components modular and reusable
- Document complex logic with clear comments

Performance Metrics
- Monitor Core Web Vitals
- Implement performance budgets
- Regular Lighthouse audits
- Monitor bundle sizes

Refer to Astro's official documentation alongside shadcn/ui documentation for detailed component implementation guidelines.
